1
00:00:01,064 --> 00:00:04,026
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,111
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:44,066
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,902
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,071
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:53,658 --> 00:00:55,494
-Thank you for the meal.
-Thank you.

7
00:00:55,577 --> 00:00:57,204
[eatery owner] Thank you, bye.

8
00:00:57,287 --> 00:00:58,789
[shop bell chimes, door opens]

9
00:00:59,539 --> 00:01:01,124
[door closes, shop bell chimes]

10
00:01:03,126 --> 00:01:04,544
EPISODE 7

11
00:01:05,128 --> 00:01:07,714
Ah! [chuckles softly]

12
00:01:07,798 --> 00:01:09,257
It's been a while.

13
00:01:09,341 --> 00:01:10,467
It has.

14
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:12,177
I missed your gukbap.

15
00:01:16,973 --> 00:01:19,601
By the way, I don't see your wife.

16
00:01:20,644 --> 00:01:23,271
She passed last year.

17
00:01:24,439 --> 00:01:25,857
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

18
00:01:25,941 --> 00:01:28,985
She said she just wanted to know

19
00:01:29,069 --> 00:01:30,821
whether our son was alive or not.

20
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:33,407
I wonder if she knows now.

21
00:01:39,246 --> 00:01:40,247
[exhales softly]

22
00:01:41,915 --> 00:01:43,250
Even now, sometimes,

23
00:01:44,418 --> 00:01:46,628
Heejun appears in my dreams.

24
00:01:48,463 --> 00:01:50,173
He's probably dead.

25
00:01:55,637 --> 00:01:56,888
Please find him.

26
00:02:01,435 --> 00:02:03,019
So I can at least hold a funeral.

27
00:02:05,814 --> 00:02:06,815
[sighs softly]

28
00:02:18,452 --> 00:02:19,870
[Changun] Joo Hyera.

29
00:02:19,953 --> 00:02:21,079
[♪ music fades]

30
00:02:27,711 --> 00:02:28,712
[sighs softly]

31
00:02:30,672 --> 00:02:31,673
Got a lot on your mind?

32
00:02:38,054 --> 00:02:39,389
Are you still after Yu Seongwon?

33
00:02:39,473 --> 00:02:42,267
YU SEONGWON RETURNS AFTER 4 YEARS
TO HOLD A SOLO EXHIBITION

34
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:44,936
That's why you came back here, isn't it?

35
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:47,230
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

36
00:02:47,314 --> 00:02:48,774
I know how you feel.

37
00:02:48,857 --> 00:02:51,151
There's always that one case
we can't forget.

38
00:02:51,234 --> 00:02:52,652
But

39
00:02:52,736 --> 00:02:54,571
we checked Yu Seongwon's alibi.

40
00:02:59,951 --> 00:03:01,495
It's become an obsession for you.

41
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,163
Huh?

42
00:03:03,246 --> 00:03:04,748
That's what ruins detectives.

43
00:03:04,831 --> 00:03:06,416
It's not an obsession.

44
00:03:07,793 --> 00:03:08,835
Yu Seongwon

45
00:03:10,504 --> 00:03:12,088
will kill again.

46
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:14,716
I'm going to stop him.

47
00:03:20,764 --> 00:03:21,973
[♪ music fades]

48
00:03:32,192 --> 00:03:33,944
[♪ ominous music playing]

49
00:04:01,221 --> 00:04:03,848
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS
STYLE
::cue()

50
00:04:07,227 --> 00:04:09,479
[♪ music increases in tempo]

51
00:04:27,831 --> 00:04:29,082
[♪ music swells]

52
00:04:36,590 --> 00:04:37,632
[Isoo] Seongwon.

53
00:04:37,716 --> 00:04:38,717
[♪ music stops]

54
00:04:39,342 --> 00:04:40,343
[Seongwon] Isoo!

55
00:04:40,427 --> 00:04:42,220
-Oh!
-[chuckles]

56
00:04:43,138 --> 00:04:45,932
[grunts] I really missed you.

57
00:04:46,016 --> 00:04:47,100
[Isoo] Me too.

58
00:04:47,183 --> 00:04:50,270
Hey, this is for you.
I've never given flowers to a guy before.

59
00:04:50,353 --> 00:04:51,771
[Seongwon chuckles]

60
00:04:52,355 --> 00:04:55,817
Whoa, you're looking
even better than before.

61
00:04:55,901 --> 00:04:56,943
It's nothing new.

62
00:04:57,027 --> 00:05:00,238
Hey, you're finally starting to look
like a professional artist now.

63
00:05:00,322 --> 00:05:01,531
-Really?
-Yeah.

64
00:05:01,615 --> 00:05:02,616
-[chuckles]
-[sighs]

65
00:05:02,699 --> 00:05:04,034
Just look at all this.

66
00:05:05,285 --> 00:05:07,162
Isoo, come this way.

67
00:05:07,245 --> 00:05:09,080
-You need to see this piece first.
-What?

68
00:05:09,164 --> 00:05:10,916
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

69
00:05:18,131 --> 00:05:19,424
[♪ music fades]

70
00:05:20,592 --> 00:05:22,510
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

71
00:05:22,594 --> 00:05:24,012
All right.

72
00:05:25,639 --> 00:05:28,016
Look closely. Nothing here, right?

73
00:05:28,099 --> 00:05:29,184
No, nothing there.

74
00:05:29,267 --> 00:05:30,810
Put your hand in and feel it.

75
00:05:32,729 --> 00:05:34,731
-There's really nothing here.
-Nothing there.

76
00:05:34,814 --> 00:05:38,276
And if I mix in a bit of magic
from Kyungjin's nose...

77
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:40,612
[exclaims, whispers] Now, let's see.

78
00:05:41,821 --> 00:05:43,865
[grunts] Oh my gosh.

79
00:05:45,033 --> 00:05:46,242
Ta-da.

80
00:05:46,326 --> 00:05:47,619
Ooh, how did you do that?

81
00:05:47,702 --> 00:05:49,162
There's a secret compartment.

82
00:05:49,245 --> 00:05:51,331
I expected a rabbit at the very least.

83
00:05:51,414 --> 00:05:54,209
[scoffs] Hey, see if there's
a secret compartment.

84
00:05:54,292 --> 00:05:55,293
As if.

85
00:05:59,255 --> 00:06:01,466
All right, in here,

86
00:06:01,549 --> 00:06:03,802
add a bit of magic from Jin Isoo's nose,

87
00:06:05,345 --> 00:06:07,347
-and voilà.
-Whoa!

88
00:06:07,430 --> 00:06:09,933
So anyone can do this.

89
00:06:10,016 --> 00:06:11,184
[scoffs softly]

90
00:06:11,434 --> 00:06:12,644
How did you know?

91
00:06:12,727 --> 00:06:15,313
It's obvious.
It's not like you have a magic pocket.

92
00:06:15,397 --> 00:06:17,440
You're such a killjoy.

93
00:06:17,524 --> 00:06:18,775
You told me to try.

94
00:06:20,694 --> 00:06:21,903
Bro.

95
00:06:22,779 --> 00:06:23,989
Park Jaeha's magic show.

96
00:06:24,072 --> 00:06:25,532
These tickets are impossible to get.

97
00:06:25,615 --> 00:06:28,034
You said you wanted to see it.
Those are VIP seats.

98
00:06:28,118 --> 00:06:29,369
What is it?

99
00:06:29,452 --> 00:06:30,495
[♪ jaunty music playing]

100
00:06:30,578 --> 00:06:33,373
Magic is basically deception, isn't it?

101
00:06:33,456 --> 00:06:34,749
[scoffs]

102
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:36,167
Deception?

103
00:06:36,251 --> 00:06:38,044
Magic is an art.

104
00:06:38,128 --> 00:06:41,172
An elevated art form
where science meets performance.

105
00:06:41,256 --> 00:06:42,257
I'm not interested.

106
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:44,384
Really? I have a ticket for Dr. Yoon, too.

107
00:06:44,467 --> 00:06:46,845
Really? Then I'll go. Thanks.

108
00:06:47,762 --> 00:06:49,889
-You bring your girlfriend, too.
-Thanks, bro.

109
00:06:52,976 --> 00:06:56,187
You can throw it away or use it
as scrap paper if you don't need it.

110
00:06:57,397 --> 00:06:58,898
I'm coming, too.

111
00:06:58,982 --> 00:07:00,066
Really?

112
00:07:00,692 --> 00:07:02,694
If you really want it, be my guest.

113
00:07:05,196 --> 00:07:06,239
[♪ music fades]

114
00:07:10,118 --> 00:07:11,745
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

115
00:07:13,163 --> 00:07:14,706
Oh, Detective Jin.

116
00:07:15,498 --> 00:07:16,583
Hey...

117
00:07:16,666 --> 00:07:19,085
Thanks for the ticket.
I really wanted to see this.

118
00:07:19,169 --> 00:07:21,755
Ah, I knew you were
a cultured person, Dr. Yoon.

119
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:24,966
-What about me?
-You're just a person.

120
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:26,760
[chuckles softly]

121
00:07:27,635 --> 00:07:28,970
[Dr. Yoon] Detective Joo.

122
00:07:29,053 --> 00:07:30,805
You look great today.

123
00:07:30,889 --> 00:07:32,807
Ah. [chuckles] Not at all.

124
00:07:32,891 --> 00:07:34,100
You look great, too.

125
00:07:34,184 --> 00:07:35,310
[chuckles softly]

126
00:07:36,728 --> 00:07:37,729
You look awful.

127
00:07:37,812 --> 00:07:38,980
Yeah, you too.

128
00:07:40,106 --> 00:07:41,232
Why is he so late?

129
00:07:41,316 --> 00:07:44,152
[sighs] I've never met
Kyungjin's girlfriend before.

130
00:07:44,235 --> 00:07:45,779
Me neither.

131
00:07:45,862 --> 00:07:48,698
Don't tease him
when his girlfriend arrives.

132
00:07:48,782 --> 00:07:51,534
When do we ever tease? We congratulate.

133
00:07:51,618 --> 00:07:52,702
[chuckles]

134
00:07:53,453 --> 00:07:54,496
[Kyungjin] Bro!

135
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:57,749
Why are you alone?
Where's your girlfriend?

136
00:07:57,832 --> 00:07:58,917
She has to work late today.

137
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,335
-Out of the blue?
-Yeah.

138
00:08:00,418 --> 00:08:02,462
She wanted to come,
but she's been busy lately.

139
00:08:03,963 --> 00:08:05,465
Too bad, then.

140
00:08:05,548 --> 00:08:07,008
Shall we head inside?

141
00:08:08,927 --> 00:08:10,512
[Isoo] You don't have a girlfriend,
do you?

142
00:08:10,595 --> 00:08:11,596
[Kyungjin] I do.

143
00:08:11,679 --> 00:08:13,306
-[Isoo] I don't think you do.
-[Kyungjin] I really do.
STYLE
::cue()

144
00:08:14,224 --> 00:08:16,184
[♪ upbeat, intriguing music playing]

145
00:08:33,034 --> 00:08:34,786
[♪ music slows]

146
00:08:34,869 --> 00:08:36,329
[♪ music resumes tempo]

147
00:08:36,412 --> 00:08:38,331
[audience cheering, applauding]

148
00:08:45,755 --> 00:08:49,717
[announcer] And now,
Park Jaeha's Magic Fire begins!

149
00:08:49,801 --> 00:08:51,886
[audience continues cheering, applauding]

150
00:09:31,342 --> 00:09:32,594
Ooh!

151
00:09:35,430 --> 00:09:37,098
[♪ music slows]

152
00:09:38,057 --> 00:09:39,726
[♪ music resumes tempo]

153
00:09:40,810 --> 00:09:42,061
[flames whooshing]

154
00:09:44,856 --> 00:09:45,940
[audience gasps]

155
00:09:48,484 --> 00:09:50,195
[audience exclaims in amazement]

156
00:09:50,278 --> 00:09:51,362
[Isoo] Whoa!

157
00:09:51,946 --> 00:09:53,656
[softly] How did he light it on fire?

158
00:09:54,407 --> 00:09:56,117
[whispering] Hey, have some manners.
[clicks tongue]

159
00:09:56,201 --> 00:09:58,077
I want to know what the trick is.

160
00:09:58,161 --> 00:10:00,163
It's not a trick. It's art.

161
00:10:00,246 --> 00:10:01,623
What's the matter with you?

162
00:10:02,624 --> 00:10:04,542
[successive electrical thuds echoing]

163
00:10:05,835 --> 00:10:07,462
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

164
00:10:13,885 --> 00:10:17,013
There is someone I love.

165
00:10:26,856 --> 00:10:28,316
She lived an unhappy life,

166
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:31,444
because her father was a violent man.

167
00:10:32,237 --> 00:10:33,321
[sighs wearily]

168
00:10:35,990 --> 00:10:37,533
[♪ dramatic sting]

169
00:10:38,159 --> 00:10:39,160
I wanted

170
00:10:41,037 --> 00:10:42,497
to make her smile.

171
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:09,357
[♪ enchanting music playing]

172
00:11:10,608 --> 00:11:11,818
-[audience exclaims in awe]
-Oh...

173
00:11:11,901 --> 00:11:12,902
What on earth?

174
00:11:12,986 --> 00:11:14,570
-Whoa!
-Whoa.

175
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:24,455
[♪ music increases in tempo]

176
00:11:54,610 --> 00:11:55,653
[gasps softly]

177
00:12:07,248 --> 00:12:09,167
[♪ music swells]

178
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,050
[♪ music fades]

179
00:12:17,842 --> 00:12:19,552
[♪ upbeat, lively
orchestral music playing]

180
00:12:38,321 --> 00:12:39,697
[audience exclaims in amazement]

181
00:12:46,662 --> 00:12:47,914
[audience applauding]

182
00:12:57,173 --> 00:12:58,508
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

183
00:13:03,137 --> 00:13:04,889
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

184
00:13:31,249 --> 00:13:33,793
-[audience exclaims in awe]
-[Isoo] Whoa.

185
00:13:34,752 --> 00:13:36,546
[♪ enchanting music playing]

186
00:13:55,773 --> 00:13:57,525
[audience exclaims in awe]

187
00:13:57,608 --> 00:13:58,693
Where is he going?

188
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:23,551
[♪ music fades]

189
00:14:24,552 --> 00:14:25,845
[gunshot]

190
00:14:29,807 --> 00:14:31,142
-Oh!
-[audience gasps]

191
00:14:31,225 --> 00:14:33,060
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

192
00:14:40,234 --> 00:14:41,611
[breath trembling]

193
00:14:43,029 --> 00:14:44,071
[flames whoosh]

194
00:14:44,155 --> 00:14:45,907
[audience gasps in shock]

195
00:14:45,990 --> 00:14:47,742
-[scattered screams]
-[♪ music fades]

196
00:14:48,701 --> 00:14:50,077
Whoa...

197
00:14:50,161 --> 00:14:51,454
Oh!

198
00:14:51,537 --> 00:14:52,622
[Junyoung] Wow.

199
00:14:53,748 --> 00:14:55,166
[fire roaring]

200
00:14:57,126 --> 00:14:58,252
[breathes shakily]

201
00:15:01,297 --> 00:15:03,382
-[flames whoosh, roar intensely]
-[audience gasps in horror]

202
00:15:03,466 --> 00:15:05,259
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

203
00:15:07,845 --> 00:15:09,555
-[burning wood crashes]
-[partner screams]

204
00:15:09,972 --> 00:15:11,182
[screaming in horror]

205
00:15:13,768 --> 00:15:14,936
Help!

206
00:15:15,019 --> 00:15:16,604
[audience exclaiming in horror]

207
00:15:18,022 --> 00:15:20,107
-Get everyone to safety first.
-Okay.

208
00:15:20,191 --> 00:15:22,360
Help! Oh my god!

209
00:15:22,443 --> 00:15:25,947
[Isoo] Everyone, it's all right.
Remain calm and follow our instructions.

210
00:15:26,030 --> 00:15:29,408
[Junyoung] Everyone, please slow down.
Please evacuate in an orderly manner.

211
00:15:30,409 --> 00:15:31,953
-[clamoring]
-Please walk slowly.

212
00:15:32,036 --> 00:15:34,497
Please evacuate in an orderly manner.

213
00:15:40,586 --> 00:15:41,754
[♪ music fades]

214
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:45,216
[Changun, over phone]
So you're saying that magician is dead?

215
00:15:45,299 --> 00:15:48,010
Yes, he died in a fire
during the performance.

216
00:15:48,678 --> 00:15:49,762
[sighs wearily]

217
00:15:50,429 --> 00:15:52,807
I'll send forensics over.
Your team will take this case.

218
00:15:52,890 --> 00:15:54,433
Yes, sir.

219
00:15:55,017 --> 00:15:56,018
[line disconnects]

220
00:15:56,102 --> 00:15:57,853
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

221
00:16:00,773 --> 00:16:02,775
How could something like this happen?

222
00:16:02,858 --> 00:16:04,110
I know.

223
00:16:07,822 --> 00:16:09,198
We're taking this case.

224
00:16:10,199 --> 00:16:13,202
If you need an autopsy, let me know.

225
00:16:13,869 --> 00:16:14,954
I'm going to go.

226
00:16:15,705 --> 00:16:16,706
I'll leave you to it.

227
00:16:20,543 --> 00:16:22,295
Let's get statements from people first.

228
00:16:22,378 --> 00:16:23,379
-Got it.
-[Kyungjin] Got it.

229
00:16:27,091 --> 00:16:28,134
[Isoo] Hmm...

230
00:16:32,763 --> 00:16:33,764
Is he...

231
00:16:33,848 --> 00:16:35,725
MAGIC PERFORMANCE PARTNER
JEONG DAHEE

232
00:16:35,808 --> 00:16:37,518
[voice shaking] Is he really dead?

233
00:16:41,564 --> 00:16:42,565
Yes.

234
00:16:44,191 --> 00:16:47,611
[sobbing] How could he die like this?

235
00:16:48,487 --> 00:16:49,822
[sniffling, sobbing]

236
00:16:54,118 --> 00:16:56,912
How long have you
worked with Mr. Park Jaeha?

237
00:16:58,247 --> 00:17:00,207
From a year ago.

238
00:17:00,958 --> 00:17:03,586
So, earlier,

239
00:17:03,669 --> 00:17:05,379
what happened to the casket?

240
00:17:06,339 --> 00:17:07,715
I don't know.

241
00:17:08,632 --> 00:17:10,760
[breath trembling] Originally,

242
00:17:10,843 --> 00:17:14,096
it was supposed to open from the back.

243
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:15,598
[♪ intriguing music playing]

244
00:17:18,142 --> 00:17:20,853
And then he's supposed to reappear.

245
00:17:20,936 --> 00:17:22,480
[♪ music increases in tempo]

246
00:17:29,195 --> 00:17:30,655
[♪ music swells]

247
00:17:37,036 --> 00:17:38,162
[audience applauding]

248
00:17:39,664 --> 00:17:40,748
[♪ music fades]

249
00:17:40,831 --> 00:17:44,669
[sobbing] I don't know how this happened.

250
00:17:45,461 --> 00:17:46,462
[Isoo sighs softly]

251
00:17:47,129 --> 00:17:48,130
[Hyera sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

252
00:17:48,923 --> 00:17:50,841
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

253
00:17:50,925 --> 00:17:52,426
[camera shutter clicking]

254
00:18:01,268 --> 00:18:03,771
What could have happened here?

255
00:18:04,897 --> 00:18:06,023
[voice shaking] I don't know.

256
00:18:06,107 --> 00:18:08,192
STAGE DIRECTOR
LEE JIYUN

257
00:18:09,193 --> 00:18:10,194
[sniffles]

258
00:18:10,277 --> 00:18:12,780
The escape mechanism worked just fine.

259
00:18:12,863 --> 00:18:14,407
He should've come down this way.

260
00:18:17,993 --> 00:18:20,204
Could there have been
a problem with the casket?

261
00:18:21,038 --> 00:18:23,582
I checked everything just before the show.

262
00:18:23,666 --> 00:18:25,376
There was nothing wrong with it.

263
00:18:25,459 --> 00:18:26,794
[♪ music swells]

264
00:18:26,877 --> 00:18:27,962
[sobbing]

265
00:18:31,006 --> 00:18:32,049
[♪ music fades]

266
00:18:32,675 --> 00:18:33,718
[Kyungjin] Detective Joo!

267
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:37,179
The escape mechanism was working.

268
00:18:38,097 --> 00:18:40,141
Then was something wrong with the casket?

269
00:18:40,224 --> 00:18:42,643
The stage director said
nothing was wrong with it.

270
00:18:42,727 --> 00:18:43,936
Who made the casket?

271
00:18:44,019 --> 00:18:45,187
An engineer made it.

272
00:18:45,271 --> 00:18:46,689
His workshop is right next door.

273
00:18:46,772 --> 00:18:48,733
Mmm. We'll go meet him.

274
00:18:48,816 --> 00:18:50,526
Okay. I'll check the security cameras.

275
00:18:54,739 --> 00:18:56,323
[woman sobbing distantly]

276
00:19:01,162 --> 00:19:02,329
What's that?

277
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:11,130
[sobbing grows louder]

278
00:19:12,006 --> 00:19:13,299
[♪ jaunty music playing]

279
00:19:13,382 --> 00:19:14,550
[sobbing stops]

280
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:21,682
TAROT MASTER
LUNA

281
00:19:28,022 --> 00:19:29,106
[electricity crackling]

282
00:19:30,274 --> 00:19:31,984
[electricity crackling]

283
00:19:34,779 --> 00:19:35,780
[♪ music fades]

284
00:19:35,863 --> 00:19:38,908
So you do tarot readings here?

285
00:19:40,910 --> 00:19:42,161
Yes.

286
00:19:42,244 --> 00:19:44,997
I do readings for people
who win the giveaway.

287
00:19:46,457 --> 00:19:48,000
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

288
00:19:48,083 --> 00:19:49,168
PARK JAEHA'S MAGIC FIRE

289
00:19:49,919 --> 00:19:51,921
Were you close with Park Jaeha?

290
00:19:55,007 --> 00:19:57,259
I told him to be careful.

291
00:19:57,343 --> 00:19:59,595
You mean you knew he was going to die?

292
00:20:00,429 --> 00:20:01,430
Yes.

293
00:20:03,432 --> 00:20:05,559
I had a dream.

294
00:20:06,268 --> 00:20:08,145
Ah. [chuckles softly] A dream?

295
00:20:08,938 --> 00:20:10,356
Like a prophetic dream?

296
00:20:11,023 --> 00:20:12,149
Yes.

297
00:20:12,233 --> 00:20:15,152
I've always had a kind of sixth sense
since I was little.

298
00:20:15,236 --> 00:20:18,948
I have prophetic dreams
before something happens.

299
00:20:19,031 --> 00:20:21,158
I even knew before my grandfather died.

300
00:20:21,242 --> 00:20:22,451
Oh...

301
00:20:23,327 --> 00:20:25,120
[Luna] But yesterday,

302
00:20:25,746 --> 00:20:26,747
I saw it.

303
00:20:28,541 --> 00:20:30,501
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

304
00:20:54,525 --> 00:20:57,361
So this morning, I told him to be careful,
and he said...

305
00:20:57,444 --> 00:20:58,445
He said?

306
00:21:00,614 --> 00:21:02,783
I have to treat it
like my last performance

307
00:21:03,659 --> 00:21:04,827
and do my best.

308
00:21:05,911 --> 00:21:06,912
Jaeha.

309
00:21:06,996 --> 00:21:08,372
Thanks, Luna.

310
00:21:12,585 --> 00:21:13,878
[♪ music fades]

311
00:21:15,963 --> 00:21:18,340
Did you see anything else in that dream?

312
00:21:22,636 --> 00:21:23,637
No.

313
00:21:23,721 --> 00:21:24,889
Oh...

314
00:21:26,307 --> 00:21:28,392
All right, thank you for your cooperation.

315
00:21:30,978 --> 00:21:33,564
Wow, that's incredible.

316
00:21:33,647 --> 00:21:35,024
She had a prophetic dream.

317
00:21:35,107 --> 00:21:36,358
[exhales softly in awe]

318
00:21:37,026 --> 00:21:39,111
You don't believe that stuff, do you?

319
00:21:39,194 --> 00:21:40,195
Of course not.

320
00:21:40,279 --> 00:21:41,322
[sighs]

321
00:21:41,405 --> 00:21:43,824
When I was learning at the police academy,

322
00:21:43,908 --> 00:21:47,578
a certain instructor said,
"Accept new information without bias."

323
00:21:50,331 --> 00:21:51,665
You must've forgotten.

324
00:21:51,749 --> 00:21:54,627
When you're investigating a case,
psychics call all the time,

325
00:21:54,710 --> 00:21:56,253
claiming they know something.

326
00:21:56,337 --> 00:21:58,964
But when you ask who did it,
they suddenly can't see it.

327
00:21:59,048 --> 00:22:00,090
[scoffs softly]

328
00:22:00,633 --> 00:22:03,093
More importantly,
what Park Jaeha said is bothering me.

329
00:22:04,053 --> 00:22:05,054
What do you mean?

330
00:22:05,137 --> 00:22:07,473
He said he had to treat it
like his last performance.

331
00:22:08,474 --> 00:22:10,267
As if he knew he would die.

332
00:22:10,351 --> 00:22:11,852
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

333
00:22:12,978 --> 00:22:15,230
I have to treat it
like my last performance

334
00:22:15,981 --> 00:22:17,483
and do my best.

335
00:22:20,402 --> 00:22:21,570
Let's go to the workshop.

336
00:22:22,529 --> 00:22:23,697
Okay.
STYLE
::cue()

337
00:22:23,781 --> 00:22:24,907
[♪ music fades]

338
00:22:26,450 --> 00:22:28,077
I assume you haven't found much.

339
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:30,079
Well, everything burned to a crisp.

340
00:22:30,746 --> 00:22:32,539
We'll check right away and let you know.

341
00:22:32,623 --> 00:22:33,874
-Okay.
-Good luck.

342
00:22:33,958 --> 00:22:35,292
-[Junyoung] Okay.
-[Kyungjin] Thank you, sir.

343
00:22:38,796 --> 00:22:39,838
[Junyoung sighs]

344
00:22:41,423 --> 00:22:42,591
What happened here?

345
00:22:43,676 --> 00:22:44,677
And you are?

346
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,345
I'm the CEO of the production company.

347
00:22:46,428 --> 00:22:47,429
SHOW PRODUCER
CHOI MIHEE

348
00:22:47,513 --> 00:22:48,639
Did Jaeha die?

349
00:22:48,722 --> 00:22:51,350
Yes, he is deceased.

350
00:22:52,643 --> 00:22:53,644
How?

351
00:22:53,727 --> 00:22:57,064
It seems there was a problem
with the magic equipment.

352
00:22:58,065 --> 00:23:00,859
That's impossible. [scoffs in disbelief]

353
00:23:14,957 --> 00:23:16,041
[Isoo] Hello?

354
00:23:20,045 --> 00:23:21,046
[door unlocks]

355
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:26,093
[low, mechanical whirring]

356
00:23:27,094 --> 00:23:29,054
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

357
00:23:33,267 --> 00:23:34,518
Mr. Park Jaeha?

358
00:23:36,270 --> 00:23:37,980
MAGIC SHOW ENGINEER
PARK JAEHYUNG

359
00:23:38,063 --> 00:23:39,398
I'm Park Jaehyung.

360
00:23:40,190 --> 00:23:41,316
Jaeha's brother.

361
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:43,527
You're twins.

362
00:23:46,905 --> 00:23:48,198
[Isoo exhales softly]

363
00:23:49,408 --> 00:23:50,576
We're with the police.

364
00:23:51,243 --> 00:23:52,286
[breath trembles]

365
00:23:52,953 --> 00:23:54,913
Did you hear the news?

366
00:23:55,539 --> 00:23:56,540
Yes.

367
00:23:57,499 --> 00:23:59,001
I heard it just now.

368
00:24:01,045 --> 00:24:02,671
Is it true?

369
00:24:02,755 --> 00:24:04,089
Yes.

370
00:24:04,173 --> 00:24:06,008
[♪ melancholy music playing]

371
00:24:08,010 --> 00:24:09,261
[chokes, sobs]

372
00:24:14,516 --> 00:24:16,018
[sobbing softly]

373
00:24:27,321 --> 00:24:28,447
[♪ music fades]

374
00:24:29,656 --> 00:24:32,201
We heard you build the equipment yourself.

375
00:24:32,284 --> 00:24:34,745
We used to perform together in the past,

376
00:24:37,081 --> 00:24:38,540
but after I injured my legs,

377
00:24:39,333 --> 00:24:40,667
I became an engineer.

378
00:24:42,544 --> 00:24:46,048
The performance you did together
must have been a teleportation act.

379
00:24:46,673 --> 00:24:47,674
That's right.

380
00:24:48,300 --> 00:24:49,676
Teleportation?

381
00:24:51,386 --> 00:24:52,721
We went to see a show,

382
00:24:53,430 --> 00:24:55,057
and the CEO scouted us.

383
00:24:59,228 --> 00:25:00,604
Because we're twins.

384
00:25:00,687 --> 00:25:02,189
[♪ intriguing music playing]

385
00:25:04,233 --> 00:25:06,151
[chain clinking, rattling]

386
00:25:17,663 --> 00:25:19,623
[♪ music swells]

387
00:25:22,209 --> 00:25:23,669
[audience gasps]

388
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:32,052
[announcer] Park Jaeha's Teleportation!

389
00:25:32,136 --> 00:25:33,262
[audience gasps]

390
00:25:33,345 --> 00:25:34,930
[audience cheering, applauding]

391
00:25:40,602 --> 00:25:41,728
-[♪ music fades]
-[Isoo] That was

392
00:25:42,771 --> 00:25:44,648
done by twins?

393
00:25:45,357 --> 00:25:46,358
Yes.

394
00:25:48,986 --> 00:25:50,445
Jaeha was talented.

395
00:25:51,155 --> 00:25:52,614
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

396
00:25:52,698 --> 00:25:54,783
So he made his professional debut,

397
00:25:56,243 --> 00:25:58,537
and I only joined him
for the teleportation act.

398
00:26:01,915 --> 00:26:04,585
What exactly happened?

399
00:26:05,878 --> 00:26:07,296
The casket caught on fire...

400
00:26:07,379 --> 00:26:08,589
[breath trembles]

401
00:26:08,672 --> 00:26:11,341
...and your brother wasn't able to escape.

402
00:26:11,425 --> 00:26:12,551
[chokes back a sob]

403
00:26:14,970 --> 00:26:16,013
[crying softly]

404
00:26:17,139 --> 00:26:19,683
[voice shaking] I kept telling him
it was dangerous.

405
00:26:21,685 --> 00:26:23,687
Are you saying the casket was dangerous?

406
00:26:23,770 --> 00:26:25,689
If the fuel leaked,

407
00:26:27,524 --> 00:26:30,944
it could cause an accident,
so I told him not to do it.

408
00:26:32,487 --> 00:26:34,364
Then why did he...

409
00:26:35,866 --> 00:26:37,951
Jaeha always said the same thing.

410
00:26:38,035 --> 00:26:40,370
Don't you know how lucky I am, Jaehyung?

411
00:26:40,454 --> 00:26:41,955
Things like that don't happen to me.

412
00:26:42,039 --> 00:26:43,123
Okay.

413
00:26:45,125 --> 00:26:47,127
It was the same
when the accident happened.

414
00:26:48,378 --> 00:26:49,838
Jaeha was fine,

415
00:26:53,550 --> 00:26:54,885
while I ended up like this.

416
00:26:55,677 --> 00:26:57,095
So I, too,

417
00:26:57,179 --> 00:26:59,765
believed that luck was on his side,
STYLE
::cue()

418
00:27:01,767 --> 00:27:03,227
but then this happened. [sobbing]

419
00:27:05,312 --> 00:27:06,897
[sniffles, continues sobbing]

420
00:27:08,607 --> 00:27:09,775
[♪ music fades]

421
00:27:09,858 --> 00:27:12,319
There's no way there was
a problem with the equipment.

422
00:27:12,402 --> 00:27:14,446
Do you know how much
we rehearse before the show?

423
00:27:14,529 --> 00:27:17,157
We run it dozens, even hundreds of times
without a problem

424
00:27:17,241 --> 00:27:18,659
before it goes on stage.

425
00:27:18,742 --> 00:27:20,244
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

426
00:27:24,331 --> 00:27:25,749
[siren wailing]

427
00:27:29,044 --> 00:27:30,212
[♪ music fades]

428
00:27:30,295 --> 00:27:33,090
The production company's CEO
insists there wasn't a problem.

429
00:27:34,049 --> 00:27:36,468
She wouldn't want to admit
that it was an accident.

430
00:27:36,551 --> 00:27:38,011
The engineer said it was dangerous.

431
00:27:38,095 --> 00:27:40,138
Hey, the engineer is the magician's twin.

432
00:27:40,222 --> 00:27:41,682
-His twin?
-[Isoo] Yeah.

433
00:27:42,641 --> 00:27:43,767
[sighs heavily]

434
00:27:43,850 --> 00:27:46,311
To think the teleportation magic
was a trick with twins.

435
00:27:46,895 --> 00:27:49,231
Obviously. Did you think
he was actually teleporting?

436
00:27:49,773 --> 00:27:51,233
Do superpowers really not exist?

437
00:27:52,943 --> 00:27:54,486
Let's go back for now.

438
00:27:54,569 --> 00:27:56,905
We'll know once
the forensic results are out.

439
00:27:56,989 --> 00:27:58,865
-Okay.
-Have a good evening.

440
00:28:02,202 --> 00:28:03,370
Mr. Innocent.

441
00:28:04,037 --> 00:28:05,747
[chuckles softly] Let's go.

442
00:28:11,336 --> 00:28:13,964
So, which do you think it is?

443
00:28:14,047 --> 00:28:16,967
I can't say for sure yet. [sighs]

444
00:28:17,843 --> 00:28:19,302
But there is something strange.

445
00:28:19,886 --> 00:28:20,887
Like what?

446
00:28:20,971 --> 00:28:22,806
If this was indeed a murder,

447
00:28:23,557 --> 00:28:25,392
why was he killed on stage?

448
00:28:25,475 --> 00:28:30,272
Why create countless witnesses
by killing him during a performance?

449
00:28:30,355 --> 00:28:34,151
If a magician dies during a performance,
it can be made to look like an accident.

450
00:28:34,234 --> 00:28:37,779
But once it's revealed to be a murder,
that narrows down the suspects.

451
00:28:37,863 --> 00:28:40,615
Only a limited number of people
have access to the equipment.

452
00:28:41,742 --> 00:28:43,577
Hmm. That's true.

453
00:28:43,660 --> 00:28:44,911
[cell phone ringing over car audio]

454
00:28:44,995 --> 00:28:45,996
Sorry, one second.

455
00:28:46,079 --> 00:28:47,581
YU SEONGWON
INCOMING CALL

456
00:28:48,415 --> 00:28:51,334
Hey, Sculptor Yu.
Did the exhibition wrap up okay?

457
00:28:51,418 --> 00:28:53,920
Yeah, it just finished,
so we're packing up now.

458
00:28:54,004 --> 00:28:56,548
[Isoo] Hey, did you sell all your pieces?
I wanted to buy one.

459
00:28:57,257 --> 00:28:58,717
I don't sell my pieces.

460
00:28:58,800 --> 00:29:00,010
I keep them all.

461
00:29:00,093 --> 00:29:02,679
[Isoo] Oh. Well, look at you, Mr. Artist.

462
00:29:02,763 --> 00:29:05,057
I guess you don't need the money.

463
00:29:05,140 --> 00:29:06,141
Isoo.

464
00:29:06,808 --> 00:29:08,435
Let's meet up soon.

465
00:29:08,518 --> 00:29:10,437
It's been a while since I was last here.

466
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:12,481
Yeah, we should. How long are you staying?

467
00:29:12,564 --> 00:29:16,276
I have another exhibition coming up,
so I'll probably be in Korea for a while.

468
00:29:16,359 --> 00:29:19,654
Got it. Then let's meet up next week.
I'll call you.

469
00:29:19,738 --> 00:29:20,906
Okay, bye.

470
00:29:20,989 --> 00:29:22,115
[line disconnects]

471
00:29:22,866 --> 00:29:24,159
That reminds me,

472
00:29:25,077 --> 00:29:26,161
you were at the exhibition.

473
00:29:26,244 --> 00:29:27,996
Just look at all this.

474
00:29:31,166 --> 00:29:33,752
Isoo, come this way.
You need to see this piece first.

475
00:29:33,835 --> 00:29:35,253
What? Which one?

476
00:29:36,505 --> 00:29:37,714
Yes, I was there.

477
00:29:38,757 --> 00:29:40,258
Do you like Yu Seongwon?

478
00:29:41,093 --> 00:29:42,803
I'm very interested in him.

479
00:29:42,886 --> 00:29:45,555
No wonder. You had
photos of his exhibition at home.

480
00:29:45,639 --> 00:29:47,390
I'm close with Seongwon.

481
00:29:49,101 --> 00:29:50,185
How do you know him?

482
00:29:50,268 --> 00:29:51,853
Uh...

483
00:29:51,937 --> 00:29:54,648
You know his family owns UBS Group, right?

484
00:29:54,731 --> 00:29:57,234
I met him at a gathering
for third-generation chaebol heirs.

485
00:29:57,317 --> 00:29:59,945
I haven't seen him much
since he moved to the UK,

486
00:30:00,028 --> 00:30:02,114
but he's completely fallen for my charms.

487
00:30:02,197 --> 00:30:03,615
He likes me so much.

488
00:30:03,698 --> 00:30:04,825
[Isoo exclaims smugly]

489
00:30:06,118 --> 00:30:08,995
If you want to meet him,
I can arrange something.

490
00:30:10,247 --> 00:30:11,248
Next time.

491
00:30:12,749 --> 00:30:13,834
Are you feeling shy?

492
00:30:16,336 --> 00:30:18,255
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

493
00:30:50,495 --> 00:30:52,956
SEWON HOSPITAL

494
00:30:53,039 --> 00:30:55,375
[medical monitor beeping steadily]

495
00:30:55,458 --> 00:30:57,294
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

496
00:30:59,796 --> 00:31:03,008
[Dr. Jinkyung] Mr. Choi Jeonghun,
we will now begin the surgery.

497
00:31:03,091 --> 00:31:04,092
All right.

498
00:31:04,176 --> 00:31:06,595
Don't worry. It's going to go well.

499
00:31:07,220 --> 00:31:09,764
Just get some sleep,
and you'll wake up healthier.

500
00:31:10,807 --> 00:31:11,808
Okay.

501
00:31:11,892 --> 00:31:13,393
We're going to put you under now.

502
00:31:14,144 --> 00:31:16,438
[anesthesiologist] We'll begin
the anesthesia now.

503
00:31:18,398 --> 00:31:21,359
[Dr. Jinkyung] Please count slowly
from one to ten.

504
00:31:21,443 --> 00:31:23,486
[Mr. Choi, muffled] One.

505
00:31:24,487 --> 00:31:26,072
Two.

506
00:31:27,616 --> 00:31:28,825
Three.

507
00:31:30,994 --> 00:31:32,078
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

508
00:31:32,162 --> 00:31:35,123
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

509
00:31:36,416 --> 00:31:39,502
[Taegyun] "The magician
who burned on stage"?

510
00:31:40,045 --> 00:31:41,171
Good grief.

511
00:31:42,756 --> 00:31:46,301
Why did we end up
with another bothersome case?

512
00:31:46,384 --> 00:31:48,178
Well...

513
00:31:48,887 --> 00:31:51,264
Team 1 happened to be on site at the time.

514
00:31:51,348 --> 00:31:52,390
"Happened to be"?

515
00:31:53,558 --> 00:31:54,935
Well... [chuckles nervously]

516
00:31:55,018 --> 00:31:57,479
Detective Jin had tickets,
so they went to see the show.

517
00:31:57,562 --> 00:31:59,022
For heaven's sake.

518
00:31:59,105 --> 00:32:00,857
What's wrong with him?

519
00:32:00,941 --> 00:32:02,776
Is he a crime magnet? Jesus Christ.

520
00:32:02,859 --> 00:32:04,486
Everywhere he goes, it's a new case.

521
00:32:05,362 --> 00:32:06,363
[knock at door]

522
00:32:06,446 --> 00:32:07,530
[Taegyun] Come in.

523
00:32:08,490 --> 00:32:10,283
Right, yes. Put that in the car.

524
00:32:11,868 --> 00:32:12,953
[sighs in exasperation]

525
00:32:13,662 --> 00:32:15,997
In any case, catch the culprit quickly.

526
00:32:16,081 --> 00:32:17,540
-Got it?
-Yes, sir.

527
00:32:17,624 --> 00:32:18,875
-Yes, sir.
-[Taegyun] Right.

528
00:32:24,297 --> 00:32:25,966
PARK JAEHA, AGE 32
RENOWNED MAGICIAN

529
00:32:26,049 --> 00:32:27,842
FOUND DEAD IN A FIRE DURING A PERFORMANCE

530
00:32:27,926 --> 00:32:29,386
ACCIDENT? OR EQUIPMENT ERROR?

531
00:32:29,469 --> 00:32:31,263
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

532
00:32:31,346 --> 00:32:33,265
FIRE BREAKS OUT DURING A FIRE ESCAPE ACT

533
00:32:38,561 --> 00:32:39,604
[inhales sharply]

534
00:32:41,856 --> 00:32:44,317
This isn't an accident.
It's a murder case.

535
00:32:46,027 --> 00:32:47,988
Kerosene was detected on the casket panel.

536
00:32:52,951 --> 00:32:54,828
They normally use a special kind of oil,

537
00:32:54,911 --> 00:32:57,831
but someone poured kerosene in it,
so the flames spread inside.

538
00:32:57,914 --> 00:32:59,833
TRACES OF KEROSENE DETECTED

539
00:32:59,916 --> 00:33:02,877
Oh, and this is
the forensic analysis of his phone.

540
00:33:05,213 --> 00:33:06,256
[Junyoung scoffs softly]

541
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:08,758
[sighs] Park Jaeha was something else.

542
00:33:08,842 --> 00:33:10,552
[scoffs] What's wrong this guy?

543
00:33:11,678 --> 00:33:12,721
Look at this.

544
00:33:15,307 --> 00:33:17,726
Let's go. They're holding
a memorial for him today.

545
00:33:17,809 --> 00:33:19,227
Okay.

546
00:33:19,936 --> 00:33:21,021
Come on.

547
00:33:21,104 --> 00:33:22,230
Let's go.

548
00:33:23,523 --> 00:33:26,401
IN MEMORY OF PARK JAEHA,
WHO GAVE US SO MANY MAGICAL MOMENTS

549
00:33:26,484 --> 00:33:29,779
THE FLAMES YOU LEFT BEHIND
STILL LIVE ON IN ALL OF US

550
00:33:30,613 --> 00:33:34,951
WE WILL FOREVER REMEMBER THE SMILE
THAT MADE US BELIEVE IN MAGIC

551
00:33:35,577 --> 00:33:37,704
THE LATE PARK JAEHA (1992-2025)

552
00:33:37,787 --> 00:33:39,664
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

553
00:33:39,748 --> 00:33:41,374
[camera shutters clicking]

554
00:33:42,959 --> 00:33:45,420
Let us have a moment of silence.

555
00:33:52,177 --> 00:33:54,054
WE WON'T FORGET THE MIRACLES YOU CREATED

556
00:33:54,137 --> 00:33:55,930
MAY YOU REST IN PEACE, JAEHA

557
00:33:59,142 --> 00:34:00,143
Thank you.

558
00:34:06,399 --> 00:34:07,484
[sniffles]

559
00:34:08,610 --> 00:34:09,861
[sighs softly]

560
00:34:09,944 --> 00:34:11,071
[♪ music fades]

561
00:34:11,946 --> 00:34:15,784
The fans wanted to pay their respects,
so we arranged this memorial.

562
00:34:15,867 --> 00:34:18,745
When can we hold the funeral?

563
00:34:18,828 --> 00:34:20,747
I think this is going to take some time.

564
00:34:22,582 --> 00:34:24,459
We believe someone murdered Mr. Park.

565
00:34:26,669 --> 00:34:29,422
Do you know anyone
who might want him dead?

566
00:34:29,506 --> 00:34:31,007
[Mihee] No, not at all.

567
00:34:31,091 --> 00:34:33,051
Jaeha was always so cheerful and kind.

568
00:34:33,134 --> 00:34:35,136
He wasn't the kind of person
anyone would hate.

569
00:34:45,772 --> 00:34:48,274
[sobbing] How could something
like this happen?

570
00:34:49,067 --> 00:34:50,777
This is just so horrible.

571
00:34:55,240 --> 00:34:56,616
[continues sobbing]

572
00:35:00,495 --> 00:35:01,871
The truth is,

573
00:35:01,955 --> 00:35:04,833
I was in a relationship with him.

574
00:35:06,042 --> 00:35:07,335
[♪ jaunty music playing]

575
00:35:09,295 --> 00:35:10,630
What are you talking about?

576
00:35:13,007 --> 00:35:14,509
It's been 50 days.

577
00:35:14,592 --> 00:35:15,635
[scoffs]

578
00:35:15,719 --> 00:35:17,178
I've dated him for over a year.

579
00:35:17,262 --> 00:35:18,680
I'm sure you just had a crush.

580
00:35:18,763 --> 00:35:21,266
You dated him?
Are you sure you didn't imagine it?

581
00:35:25,603 --> 00:35:27,063
Jaeha bought this for me.
STYLE
::cue()

582
00:35:27,147 --> 00:35:28,690
-[scoffs] Me too.
-Me too.

583
00:35:32,152 --> 00:35:33,445
[Jiyun] He bought it for you?

584
00:35:34,446 --> 00:35:35,488
No way.

585
00:35:36,364 --> 00:35:37,866
I'm sure it was as a thank-you.

586
00:35:39,033 --> 00:35:40,577
You're the one who's delusional.

587
00:35:40,660 --> 00:35:42,662
Jaeha has really high standards.

588
00:35:42,746 --> 00:35:44,706
Yeah, you're way older than him, too.

589
00:35:44,789 --> 00:35:46,875
What does age have to do with anything?

590
00:35:46,958 --> 00:35:48,752
He called you immature and tacky.

591
00:35:48,835 --> 00:35:49,919
[scoffs]

592
00:35:50,003 --> 00:35:51,379
You mean "pure and innocent."

593
00:35:51,463 --> 00:35:54,007
He said he discovered true love
only after meeting me.

594
00:35:54,090 --> 00:35:55,884
[scoffs] We kept it a secret,

595
00:35:55,967 --> 00:35:59,345
but we were going to get married
next year.

596
00:35:59,429 --> 00:36:02,474
We were looking
for a place to move in together

597
00:36:02,557 --> 00:36:04,851
-and register our marriage next month.
-Marriage?

598
00:36:07,645 --> 00:36:08,938
[sighs deeply]

599
00:36:09,022 --> 00:36:10,607
There's no way.

600
00:36:10,690 --> 00:36:12,650
Why would he be into you two?

601
00:36:12,734 --> 00:36:14,861
What? Watch what you say.

602
00:36:14,944 --> 00:36:16,196
You watch what you say.

603
00:36:16,279 --> 00:36:18,531
Don't say whatever you want
just because he's dead!

604
00:36:18,615 --> 00:36:20,658
-Hey!
-[Dahee] Move in together? As if.

605
00:36:21,826 --> 00:36:24,412
I'm the one Jaeha truly loved.

606
00:36:24,496 --> 00:36:26,080
It's neither of you.

607
00:36:26,164 --> 00:36:28,208
I'm the one he chose in the end.

608
00:36:28,291 --> 00:36:31,085
He told me you stalked him.

609
00:36:31,961 --> 00:36:33,588
How dare you! Come here.

610
00:36:33,671 --> 00:36:36,466
[Isoo] Wait, hold on. Break it up.

611
00:36:36,549 --> 00:36:38,134
Violence is wrong.

612
00:36:38,218 --> 00:36:39,219
[Dahee] What do you want?

613
00:36:39,302 --> 00:36:41,554
We're in the middle
of something important.

614
00:36:41,638 --> 00:36:43,765
I know. It sounds pretty serious.

615
00:36:43,848 --> 00:36:46,518
But that something important is
pointless now.

616
00:36:46,601 --> 00:36:48,895
I checked Mr. Park Jaeha's phone records.

617
00:36:49,854 --> 00:36:50,980
Uh...

618
00:36:52,690 --> 00:36:54,150
-Jiyun?
-Yes.

619
00:36:54,234 --> 00:36:56,903
-You're "Honey 1."
-What?

620
00:36:56,986 --> 00:36:58,404
-And Dahee.
-Yes?

621
00:36:58,488 --> 00:37:00,573
-You're "Honey 2."
-What?

622
00:37:01,282 --> 00:37:02,283
-Luna?
-Yes?

623
00:37:02,367 --> 00:37:03,868
You're "Honey 6."

624
00:37:05,119 --> 00:37:06,120
Six?

625
00:37:08,414 --> 00:37:10,208
What's that supposed to mean?

626
00:37:11,084 --> 00:37:13,586
It means
Mr. Park Jaeha had a lot of girlfriends.

627
00:37:13,670 --> 00:37:17,257
In other words, you were all his honeys.

628
00:37:17,340 --> 00:37:19,509
There were seven honeys in total.

629
00:37:19,592 --> 00:37:21,845
[whispering] He must have
so much love to give.

630
00:37:21,928 --> 00:37:24,222
[stuttering] Seven people?

631
00:37:24,305 --> 00:37:26,933
Didn't you always go on dates
on the same day each week?

632
00:37:27,767 --> 00:37:28,935
Seven women, seven days.

633
00:37:29,018 --> 00:37:31,271
It must be Monday, Tuesday, and Saturday.

634
00:37:33,189 --> 00:37:34,816
Hold on.

635
00:37:36,484 --> 00:37:38,987
These are all fakes.
You lent him money too, right?

636
00:37:39,070 --> 00:37:41,114
-[gasps]
-Let's talk at the station.

637
00:37:42,115 --> 00:37:44,117
-Detective Park.
-Yes.

638
00:37:45,243 --> 00:37:46,536
-[Isoo] Let's go.
-[sighs]

639
00:37:46,619 --> 00:37:48,204
-[Junyoung] Come on.
-Just for some small talk.

640
00:37:48,288 --> 00:37:50,582
It's part of the investigation.
Come on, honeys.

641
00:37:50,665 --> 00:37:52,542
Let's talk at the station.

642
00:37:56,629 --> 00:37:58,006
[♪ music fades]

643
00:38:00,884 --> 00:38:01,968
Murder?

644
00:38:03,261 --> 00:38:04,262
You mean...

645
00:38:05,221 --> 00:38:07,307
someone killed Jaeha?

646
00:38:07,932 --> 00:38:08,933
Yes.

647
00:38:09,726 --> 00:38:12,896
Someone poured kerosene inside the casket.

648
00:38:12,979 --> 00:38:13,980
Who?

649
00:38:15,148 --> 00:38:18,693
Do you know if there was anyone
who wanted to kill your brother?

650
00:38:21,571 --> 00:38:23,698
If anyone comes to mind, please tell us.

651
00:38:25,617 --> 00:38:26,618
No.

652
00:38:27,410 --> 00:38:29,579
Jaeha was the type of person

653
00:38:30,663 --> 00:38:32,290
who was always in the spotlight.

654
00:38:32,832 --> 00:38:34,584
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

655
00:38:37,003 --> 00:38:38,421
[applauding]

656
00:38:46,471 --> 00:38:48,681
Everyone loved him.

657
00:38:49,390 --> 00:38:51,476
A little too much, I think.

658
00:38:51,559 --> 00:38:52,810
Sorry?

659
00:38:52,894 --> 00:38:56,606
We've confirmed
that Mr. Park had seven girlfriends.

660
00:38:56,689 --> 00:38:58,191
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

661
00:38:59,359 --> 00:39:01,069
He was always popular.

662
00:39:01,945 --> 00:39:04,489
It wasn't that he was popular.
He was a womanizer.

663
00:39:05,114 --> 00:39:06,783
He dated seven women at once.

664
00:39:07,700 --> 00:39:10,119
Was he in trouble at all
because of a woman?

665
00:39:10,203 --> 00:39:11,704
Did he say anything of the sort?

666
00:39:13,998 --> 00:39:14,999
No.

667
00:39:16,918 --> 00:39:18,086
[sighs softly]

668
00:39:19,379 --> 00:39:20,421
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

669
00:39:20,505 --> 00:39:22,632
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

670
00:39:23,341 --> 00:39:26,052
[Dahee] He said it'd be awkward
if other people found out,

671
00:39:26,678 --> 00:39:28,429
and that we should keep it a secret.

672
00:39:28,513 --> 00:39:30,890
Workplace relationships are never easy.

673
00:39:31,808 --> 00:39:32,850
[clears throat]

674
00:39:33,935 --> 00:39:36,104
Did you really not know he was cheating?

675
00:39:37,730 --> 00:39:38,731
Uh...

676
00:39:39,983 --> 00:39:42,318
I did notice something that felt off.

677
00:39:42,819 --> 00:39:44,779
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

678
00:39:50,868 --> 00:39:52,245
[both chuckle softly]

679
00:39:59,711 --> 00:40:01,254
You're upset with me, aren't you?

680
00:40:02,422 --> 00:40:04,632
It's just weird.

681
00:40:04,716 --> 00:40:07,719
We're just good friends
because we've worked together for so long.

682
00:40:08,511 --> 00:40:09,887
I have this beautiful,

683
00:40:10,596 --> 00:40:13,516
adorable girlfriend,
so why would I look at anyone else?

684
00:40:15,059 --> 00:40:16,060
[scoffs incredulously]

685
00:40:16,894 --> 00:40:17,895
Wait.

686
00:40:18,604 --> 00:40:19,605
You're blinding me.

687
00:40:21,024 --> 00:40:22,025
[scoffs]

688
00:40:23,609 --> 00:40:25,236
When I look into your eyes,

689
00:40:26,738 --> 00:40:27,864
I see diamonds.

690
00:40:32,326 --> 00:40:33,411
[squeals]

691
00:40:33,494 --> 00:40:34,495
And it's right here.

692
00:40:36,289 --> 00:40:37,582
Oh my god!

693
00:40:39,167 --> 00:40:40,835
When did you prepare this?

694
00:40:41,502 --> 00:40:42,545
It's nothing much.

695
00:40:43,838 --> 00:40:45,048
[softly] Ah...

696
00:40:45,131 --> 00:40:46,299
[Jaeha chuckles softly]

697
00:40:47,050 --> 00:40:49,093
-[keyboard clacking]
-[♪ music fades]

698
00:40:49,177 --> 00:40:52,388
[Junyoung] "When I look into your eyes,
I see diamonds."

699
00:40:52,472 --> 00:40:56,267
So that's the kind of thing
women like to hear.

700
00:40:58,019 --> 00:40:59,604
He was really affectionate.

701
00:41:00,104 --> 00:41:01,397
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

702
00:41:01,481 --> 00:41:03,066
Your pretty hands are all beat up.

703
00:41:03,816 --> 00:41:04,817
It's fine.

704
00:41:04,901 --> 00:41:07,278
-Want me to show you my new magic trick?
-Yes.

705
00:41:14,494 --> 00:41:15,745
It's a ring.

706
00:41:16,829 --> 00:41:17,872
It's beautiful.

707
00:41:21,417 --> 00:41:22,627
[Jiyun gasps]

708
00:41:24,212 --> 00:41:25,213
Oh my god.

709
00:41:26,422 --> 00:41:27,423
That's amazing.

710
00:41:28,049 --> 00:41:29,133
[gasps softly]

711
00:41:34,138 --> 00:41:35,139
Where did it go?

712
00:41:51,405 --> 00:41:52,406
[chuckles softly]

713
00:41:52,490 --> 00:41:53,658
Will you marry me?

714
00:41:56,577 --> 00:41:57,745
[whimpers softly]

715
00:41:59,288 --> 00:42:01,707
-[patron 1] Congratulations.
-[patron 2] Way to go.

716
00:42:01,791 --> 00:42:02,792
[patron 3] Congratulations.

717
00:42:02,875 --> 00:42:04,460
[patrons cheering, applauding]

718
00:42:05,670 --> 00:42:07,296
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

719
00:42:09,465 --> 00:42:10,716
JAEHA "WILL YOU MARRY ME?"

720
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:13,803
Getting down on your knees
and proposing in a public place

721
00:42:13,886 --> 00:42:15,847
is something women hate, isn't it?

722
00:42:15,930 --> 00:42:17,306
It depends on the person.

723
00:42:17,890 --> 00:42:19,100
[whispering] He's new to dating.

724
00:42:20,476 --> 00:42:22,019
But I was still number one,

725
00:42:22,103 --> 00:42:24,063
so he must have liked me best, right?

726
00:42:24,147 --> 00:42:26,816
-You were just the longest.
-[keyboard clacking]

727
00:42:26,899 --> 00:42:28,359
[♪ jaunty music playing]

728
00:42:28,442 --> 00:42:29,861
[sighs in exasperation]

729
00:42:29,944 --> 00:42:32,155
I thought it was destiny.

730
00:42:32,947 --> 00:42:34,323
Pick a card.

731
00:42:38,703 --> 00:42:39,996
[both gasp softly]

732
00:42:40,079 --> 00:42:41,330
Once more.

733
00:42:43,416 --> 00:42:45,585
[Jaeha hums drumroll, chuckles]

734
00:42:47,753 --> 00:42:49,130
[both] Oh!

735
00:42:49,213 --> 00:42:50,798
-What on earth?
-One last time.

736
00:42:53,759 --> 00:42:54,760
[Jaeha] Oh!

737
00:42:54,844 --> 00:42:56,012
How did you do it?
STYLE
::cue()

738
00:42:56,971 --> 00:42:58,181
[Jaeha chuckles]

739
00:42:58,264 --> 00:42:59,724
I didn't do anything.

740
00:42:59,807 --> 00:43:01,434
I told you, it's destiny.

741
00:43:02,977 --> 00:43:04,103
Oh, you.

742
00:43:04,187 --> 00:43:06,689
Why did he say he needed to borrow money?

743
00:43:06,772 --> 00:43:08,733
He said he needed it for his brother.

744
00:43:08,816 --> 00:43:09,942
For a car accident.

745
00:43:10,026 --> 00:43:11,277
To get a place to live.

746
00:43:11,360 --> 00:43:13,321
He said he'd pay it back quickly.

747
00:43:13,905 --> 00:43:15,573
-[exhales deeply]
-[sighs thoughtfully]

748
00:43:17,200 --> 00:43:18,409
[♪ music fades]

749
00:43:19,410 --> 00:43:20,620
How much did you lend him?

750
00:43:22,121 --> 00:43:23,789
-Two hundred thousand?
-Two million won.

751
00:43:23,873 --> 00:43:25,666
-Are you crazy?
-[sighs softly]

752
00:43:25,750 --> 00:43:27,293
I even cashed out my savings.

753
00:43:27,376 --> 00:43:29,086
DETECTIVE DIVISION

754
00:43:34,175 --> 00:43:35,885
[♪ jaunty, dramatic music playing]

755
00:43:41,098 --> 00:43:43,226
NATIONAL POLICE AGENCY

756
00:43:53,694 --> 00:43:55,529
Let's go have some soju.

757
00:43:56,614 --> 00:43:59,325
And think about
how to exhume and desecrate him.

758
00:43:59,408 --> 00:44:01,452
What does that mean?

759
00:44:03,204 --> 00:44:05,873
It means taking him out of the grave
and killing him again.

760
00:44:10,586 --> 00:44:11,671
[♪ music fades]

761
00:44:12,713 --> 00:44:14,090
Even so,

762
00:44:15,258 --> 00:44:18,678
would they have killed him for cheating?

763
00:44:19,553 --> 00:44:21,597
He was cheating on seven people.

764
00:44:21,681 --> 00:44:23,891
Any one of them
could've been angry enough.

765
00:44:23,975 --> 00:44:25,017
Oh.

766
00:44:26,435 --> 00:44:28,062
They won't have known.

767
00:44:30,106 --> 00:44:32,108
Jaeha can be quite meticulous.

768
00:44:32,775 --> 00:44:35,027
Then who could it be?

769
00:44:35,111 --> 00:44:37,196
[♪ suspenseful, melancholy music playing]

770
00:44:39,615 --> 00:44:40,616
[voice shaking] I honestly...

771
00:44:43,452 --> 00:44:44,662
have no idea.

772
00:44:46,622 --> 00:44:48,416
I know him best.

773
00:44:49,041 --> 00:44:51,168
He's not the type of person
anyone would hate.

774
00:44:52,545 --> 00:44:53,838
Who in the world...

775
00:44:56,590 --> 00:44:58,551
could have done such a horrible thing?

776
00:44:59,510 --> 00:45:00,511
I really,

777
00:45:02,263 --> 00:45:03,848
honestly don't know.

778
00:45:04,307 --> 00:45:05,349
[sobs]

779
00:45:05,433 --> 00:45:06,517
[sighs heavily]

780
00:45:07,310 --> 00:45:08,394
[thud]

781
00:45:09,812 --> 00:45:11,147
-[gasps]
-[dove cooing]

782
00:45:11,230 --> 00:45:12,690
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

783
00:45:14,817 --> 00:45:16,319
-[air hisses]
-[gasps, yelps]

784
00:45:26,412 --> 00:45:27,705
[in English] Magic show.

785
00:45:29,582 --> 00:45:31,334
[in Korean] You shouldn't touch anything.

786
00:45:32,209 --> 00:45:34,837
There's a lot of interesting things here.

787
00:45:42,928 --> 00:45:44,096
[♪ music fades]

788
00:45:49,935 --> 00:45:50,936
He's the killer.

789
00:45:51,020 --> 00:45:53,314
What? Where did that come from?

790
00:45:53,397 --> 00:45:54,899
He was about to get up just now.

791
00:45:55,649 --> 00:45:56,650
I didn't see it.

792
00:45:56,734 --> 00:45:58,736
You're not very observant for a detective.

793
00:45:58,819 --> 00:46:01,697
I was too busy being embarrassed
by your dove flying act.

794
00:46:01,781 --> 00:46:03,532
I saw it with my own two eyes.

795
00:46:03,616 --> 00:46:04,992
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

796
00:46:05,451 --> 00:46:06,702
[gasps]

797
00:46:08,996 --> 00:46:10,539
Maybe his legs have healed.

798
00:46:11,207 --> 00:46:13,417
He hid that fact and killed his brother.

799
00:46:14,251 --> 00:46:16,045
-Why?
-His motive was

800
00:46:17,380 --> 00:46:18,547
jealousy.

801
00:46:19,131 --> 00:46:20,800
They're twins,

802
00:46:20,883 --> 00:46:23,761
but Jaeha lived the high life,
doing magic and cheating on women.

803
00:46:23,844 --> 00:46:26,430
Whereas he's stuck in a wheelchair.

804
00:46:28,224 --> 00:46:29,308
[sighs deeply]
STYLE
::cue()

805
00:46:30,101 --> 00:46:33,020
LOVER'S REVENGE?
PARK JAEHA, HONEY 1 LEE JIYUN

806
00:46:33,104 --> 00:46:34,397
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

807
00:46:34,480 --> 00:46:36,982
HONEY 2 JEONG DAHEE, HONEY 6 LUNA

808
00:46:39,276 --> 00:46:41,695
STAGE DIRECTOR,
PERFORMANCE PARTNER, TAROT MASTER

809
00:46:41,779 --> 00:46:44,281
I don't think the three of them
knew he was cheating.

810
00:46:45,366 --> 00:46:47,701
-You sure they're not acting?
-Didn't seem like it.

811
00:46:49,203 --> 00:46:51,122
-Did you check on the kerosene?
-[Kyungjin] Yes.

812
00:46:51,205 --> 00:46:53,332
I called all the gas stations
near the theater,

813
00:46:53,416 --> 00:46:55,418
but no one's bought kerosene recently.

814
00:46:56,168 --> 00:46:57,545
PARK JAEHYUNG

815
00:46:58,129 --> 00:46:59,130
What about his brother?

816
00:46:59,213 --> 00:47:01,382
He says there isn't anyone
who'd want to kill him.

817
00:47:01,465 --> 00:47:04,051
INVOLVED WITH MULTIPLE WOMEN
SIGNS OF FINANCIAL EXPLOITATION

818
00:47:04,135 --> 00:47:06,011
He also didn't know he was a cheater.

819
00:47:07,471 --> 00:47:10,474
[sighs wearily] I really think
the brother is suspicious.

820
00:47:10,558 --> 00:47:11,559
-[♪ music fades]
-What do you mean?

821
00:47:11,642 --> 00:47:13,936
I made a dove fly out earlier.

822
00:47:15,312 --> 00:47:17,189
-A dove?
-Why?

823
00:47:17,273 --> 00:47:18,482
While stumbling around.

824
00:47:18,566 --> 00:47:21,318
It's an investigative technique. Look.

825
00:47:21,402 --> 00:47:22,945
I made the dove... You do it.

826
00:47:23,028 --> 00:47:25,156
I made the dove fly out like this,

827
00:47:25,239 --> 00:47:27,783
then Mr. Park Jaehyung
suddenly flinched like this.

828
00:47:28,784 --> 00:47:29,827
[scoffs]

829
00:47:29,910 --> 00:47:31,162
[Kyungjin] Then, you mean

830
00:47:31,245 --> 00:47:32,580
he's able to walk?

831
00:47:32,663 --> 00:47:33,914
Exactly.

832
00:47:33,998 --> 00:47:35,458
No way.

833
00:47:35,541 --> 00:47:39,378
I think he's able to walk, but pretended
not to and killed his brother.

834
00:47:41,881 --> 00:47:44,341
[sighs] Do you agree with him,
Detective Joo?

835
00:47:45,718 --> 00:47:46,760
I don't know.

836
00:47:48,554 --> 00:47:50,556
Let's check the outside security footage.

837
00:47:50,639 --> 00:47:51,765
Okay.

838
00:47:51,849 --> 00:47:53,225
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

839
00:47:53,309 --> 00:47:55,853
[inhales deeply, exhales]

840
00:47:58,772 --> 00:48:00,274
[mouse clicking]

841
00:48:08,574 --> 00:48:11,202
Ms. Lee Jiyun said
nothing was wrong with the casket, right?

842
00:48:11,285 --> 00:48:14,330
Yes, she last checked around 4:30 p.m.

843
00:48:24,340 --> 00:48:25,716
Oh, there's the casket.

844
00:48:35,851 --> 00:48:36,852
[in English] Okay.

845
00:48:37,478 --> 00:48:39,980
[in Korean] She checked the casket
at 4:30 p.m.

846
00:48:40,064 --> 00:48:41,815
The show started at 5:00 p.m.

847
00:48:41,899 --> 00:48:44,193
The fire broke out at 5:50 p.m.

848
00:48:44,276 --> 00:48:48,364
If Mr. Park Jaehyung messed with
the equipment after Ms. Lee checked it,

849
00:48:48,447 --> 00:48:51,492
he would've left the workshop
between 4:30 and 5:50 p.m.

850
00:48:55,788 --> 00:48:58,499
I heard they return the equipment
to the workshop after the show.

851
00:49:14,306 --> 00:49:18,435
Ah, when we went,
Mr. Park Jaehyung was inside the workshop.

852
00:49:18,519 --> 00:49:19,770
He never left.

853
00:49:19,853 --> 00:49:22,606
That's the only way out
for someone in a wheelchair.

854
00:49:23,774 --> 00:49:25,985
My gut tells me it's him.

855
00:49:26,068 --> 00:49:28,904
If, just like I said,

856
00:49:29,905 --> 00:49:33,033
he could walk, he can crawl
out of the window and go around.

857
00:49:33,117 --> 00:49:34,118
And avoid the cameras.

858
00:49:34,201 --> 00:49:35,536
You're obsessing again.

859
00:49:36,161 --> 00:49:37,329
My gut's telling me.

860
00:49:39,206 --> 00:49:42,501
-Let's investigate the brother too.
-See? She trusts my instincts.

861
00:49:42,585 --> 00:49:43,836
It's just to check.

862
00:49:44,378 --> 00:49:46,589
Then I'll look into him tomorrow.

863
00:49:46,672 --> 00:49:47,881
[Hyera] Okay.

864
00:49:48,799 --> 00:49:49,800
Hey.

865
00:49:49,883 --> 00:49:51,719
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

866
00:49:53,178 --> 00:49:56,682
Could Ms. Lee Jiyun
and Mr. Park Jaehyung be accomplices?

867
00:49:58,142 --> 00:50:00,978
A betrayed woman
and a jealous brother working together.

868
00:50:03,230 --> 00:50:07,026
[♪ music fades]

869
00:50:07,109 --> 00:50:08,777
-I'm going home.
-Me too.

870
00:50:08,861 --> 00:50:10,738
Hey, I'm not done explaining my theory.

871
00:50:10,821 --> 00:50:12,156
[Hyera] You should go home, too.

872
00:50:12,239 --> 00:50:13,657
[♪ jaunty music plays]

873
00:50:17,870 --> 00:50:19,788
SEWON HOSPITAL

874
00:50:28,881 --> 00:50:29,882
[knock on door]

875
00:50:32,426 --> 00:50:34,219
-[gasps] Ah.
-[door closes]

876
00:50:36,597 --> 00:50:37,598
How are you feeling?

877
00:50:38,265 --> 00:50:40,809
I'm doing better than I thought.

878
00:50:40,893 --> 00:50:42,811
That's always the case.

879
00:50:42,895 --> 00:50:44,688
Thinking about it is the scariest part.

880
00:50:44,772 --> 00:50:47,566
Once it's over,
you realize it's not so bad after all.

881
00:50:47,650 --> 00:50:49,193
That happens quite often.

882
00:50:49,276 --> 00:50:51,153
[chuckles] You're right.

883
00:50:52,529 --> 00:50:54,531
I heard you're the chairman of a company,
STYLE
::cue()

884
00:50:54,615 --> 00:50:55,741
but it's been so quiet.

885
00:50:56,867 --> 00:50:58,077
Uh...

886
00:50:58,160 --> 00:51:00,704
I didn't want to bother my staff,
so I didn't tell them.

887
00:51:01,330 --> 00:51:02,706
I just took time off work.

888
00:51:02,790 --> 00:51:03,957
What about your wife?

889
00:51:04,041 --> 00:51:06,251
I'm not married.

890
00:51:07,044 --> 00:51:08,545
I never got the chance.

891
00:51:08,629 --> 00:51:10,005
That's wise of you.

892
00:51:11,173 --> 00:51:12,800
I've been there.

893
00:51:13,008 --> 00:51:14,218
[sighs regretfully]

894
00:51:14,301 --> 00:51:16,345
-[chuckling]
-Ah. [chuckles softly]

895
00:51:17,096 --> 00:51:19,556
But you must feel lonely
being by yourself at night.

896
00:51:19,640 --> 00:51:21,183
Well,

897
00:51:21,266 --> 00:51:22,893
it's nice and quiet. [chuckles]

898
00:51:22,976 --> 00:51:24,311
I understand.

899
00:51:24,395 --> 00:51:26,647
Get plenty of sleep.
That's the best medicine.

900
00:51:26,730 --> 00:51:27,940
[chuckles]

901
00:51:28,023 --> 00:51:29,608
Call for us if you're in pain.

902
00:51:29,692 --> 00:51:31,318
I will. [chuckles]

903
00:51:31,402 --> 00:51:33,362
-Go on home.
-All right.

904
00:51:34,071 --> 00:51:35,072
Bye.

905
00:51:37,241 --> 00:51:38,283
[door opens]

906
00:51:41,328 --> 00:51:42,913
-[door closes]
-[exhales in relief]

907
00:51:43,831 --> 00:51:48,293
It's 11:00 p.m. on October 12, 2023,
at Jangseon-dong.

908
00:51:48,377 --> 00:51:50,546
October 12.

909
00:51:50,629 --> 00:51:52,965
JANGSEON-DONG DUI COLLISION
INVESTIGATION REPORT

910
00:51:53,048 --> 00:51:54,717
-Seongjun.
-Yes?

911
00:51:54,800 --> 00:51:57,010
You responded to this accident, right?

912
00:51:57,094 --> 00:51:58,429
The one with the twins.

913
00:51:58,512 --> 00:52:00,305
-[Seongjun] Yes, I did.
-What happened?

914
00:52:00,389 --> 00:52:02,015
A vehicle crashed into a building.

915
00:52:02,099 --> 00:52:03,934
The driver was heavily intoxicated.

916
00:52:04,017 --> 00:52:05,686
Who was the driver?

917
00:52:05,769 --> 00:52:07,980
It was the younger of the twins.

918
00:52:08,063 --> 00:52:09,189
Mr. Park Jaeha.

919
00:52:09,273 --> 00:52:10,858
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

920
00:52:10,941 --> 00:52:12,860
It's funny how luck works.

921
00:52:12,943 --> 00:52:16,405
The drunk driver wasn't even wearing
a seatbelt, but he was completely fine,

922
00:52:16,488 --> 00:52:18,323
whereas his brother was badly hurt.

923
00:52:23,078 --> 00:52:24,371
[♪ music swells, fades]

924
00:52:24,455 --> 00:52:27,499
Mr. Park Jaehyung has
a traumatic spinal cord injury,

925
00:52:27,583 --> 00:52:28,709
so he is unable to walk.

926
00:52:29,918 --> 00:52:32,379
Is there any chance,

927
00:52:32,463 --> 00:52:33,797
even the slightest chance,

928
00:52:34,673 --> 00:52:37,551
that he could miraculously stand up
and walk again?

929
00:52:37,634 --> 00:52:38,886
Not even a tiny chance?

930
00:52:38,969 --> 00:52:41,388
If a miracle happened, he could walk.

931
00:52:42,181 --> 00:52:44,183
That's what a miracle is, isn't it?

932
00:52:45,851 --> 00:52:47,478
Right. That's true.

933
00:52:47,561 --> 00:52:49,521
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

934
00:52:49,605 --> 00:52:51,023
[sighs wearily]

935
00:52:56,153 --> 00:52:57,154
That looks suspicious.

936
00:52:57,821 --> 00:52:58,822
[Hyera] It does.

937
00:53:00,282 --> 00:53:02,034
-Check who owns the vehicle.
-Okay.

938
00:53:02,618 --> 00:53:03,786
[keyboard clacking]

939
00:53:03,869 --> 00:53:05,496
VEHICLE REGISTRATION SEARCH

940
00:53:05,579 --> 00:53:06,997
[♪ music increases in tempo]

941
00:53:10,417 --> 00:53:12,461
OWNER HAM SEONGWOOK

942
00:53:14,213 --> 00:53:15,422
Ham Seongwook.

943
00:53:17,674 --> 00:53:18,675
He did have a motive.

944
00:53:19,718 --> 00:53:22,262
Park Jaeha crashed the car
while driving drunk,

945
00:53:22,346 --> 00:53:23,847
and his brother was injured.

946
00:53:24,431 --> 00:53:26,016
[Isoo clicks tongue, inhales deeply]

947
00:53:26,099 --> 00:53:28,560
That accident left him paralyzed
from the waist down.

948
00:53:28,644 --> 00:53:30,187
Is there a chance he could walk?

949
00:53:30,270 --> 00:53:31,271
Yes.

950
00:53:33,232 --> 00:53:34,608
-If a miracle happened.
-[♪ music fades]

951
00:53:34,691 --> 00:53:35,943
Oh, come on.

952
00:53:37,402 --> 00:53:38,987
Anyway, come look at this.

953
00:53:39,071 --> 00:53:41,073
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

954
00:53:45,285 --> 00:53:46,328
[keyboard key clacks]

955
00:53:47,371 --> 00:53:49,122
[Hyera] This is three days
before the incident.

956
00:53:52,334 --> 00:53:53,335
[keyboard key clacks]

957
00:53:53,418 --> 00:53:55,462
The vehicle is owned by Ham Seongwook.

958
00:53:56,630 --> 00:53:58,841
Ham Seongwook?
You mean that Ham Seongwook?

959
00:53:58,924 --> 00:53:59,925
Yes.

960
00:54:00,968 --> 00:54:02,135
I thought he retired.

961
00:54:03,136 --> 00:54:05,556
I thought so too, but maybe not.

962
00:54:06,640 --> 00:54:07,850
Who's Ham Seongwook?

963
00:54:07,933 --> 00:54:10,769
He's the boss of Hammurabi,
the biggest crime syndicate in Seoul.

964
00:54:11,520 --> 00:54:13,021
[victim whimpers, mutters]

965
00:54:13,105 --> 00:54:14,773
[yelping in terror]

966
00:54:14,857 --> 00:54:16,567
[breathing frantically]

967
00:54:18,110 --> 00:54:21,530
FORMER BOSS OF HAMMURABI CLAN
HAM SEONGWOOK

968
00:54:21,613 --> 00:54:23,198
[♪ music increases in tempo]

969
00:54:26,410 --> 00:54:27,578
-[blunt thud]
-[victim exclaims]

970
00:54:27,661 --> 00:54:28,662
[♪ music fades]

971
00:54:28,745 --> 00:54:32,332
He got 12 years for soliciting murder,
and he's been quiet since he got out.

972
00:54:32,416 --> 00:54:34,376
What would a gangster want
with a magician?

973
00:54:34,459 --> 00:54:36,336
We'll have to find out.

974
00:54:40,007 --> 00:54:41,341
Oh!

975
00:54:41,425 --> 00:54:44,886
There were some guys who looked like
thugs sitting behind us at the theater.

976
00:54:44,970 --> 00:54:46,680
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

977
00:54:48,223 --> 00:54:50,100
[whispering] Please stop
kicking my seat, okay?

978
00:54:50,183 --> 00:54:51,727
[softly] Are your legs too long?

979
00:54:53,061 --> 00:54:54,187
Yeah, you're right.

980
00:54:55,147 --> 00:54:57,274
They were there
on the day of the incident.

981
00:54:58,275 --> 00:54:59,276
[keyboard clacks]

982
00:55:01,486 --> 00:55:02,529
[keyboard key clacks]

983
00:55:03,196 --> 00:55:06,700
Let's find out where Ham Seongwook is
and also identify those thugs.

984
00:55:06,783 --> 00:55:08,243
-Got it.
-[Kyungjin] Got it.

985
00:55:08,869 --> 00:55:10,996
-Do you remember their faces?
-Of course.

986
00:55:11,079 --> 00:55:12,623
They had terrible manners.

987
00:55:13,999 --> 00:55:15,125
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

988
00:55:15,208 --> 00:55:18,128
[Isoo sighs] Look at these faces.
They look mean as hell.

989
00:55:19,171 --> 00:55:21,590
You really can tell a lot from a face.

990
00:55:21,673 --> 00:55:22,799
Any idea who they are?

991
00:55:22,883 --> 00:55:24,885
Mmm-mmm. Not in the slightest.

992
00:55:26,011 --> 00:55:27,220
Look at them.

993
00:55:28,430 --> 00:55:30,849
They all look the same. [sighs softly]

994
00:55:33,268 --> 00:55:34,603
Detective Joo!

995
00:55:34,686 --> 00:55:37,147
I found out how Ham Seongwook
and Park Jaeha know each other.

996
00:55:37,230 --> 00:55:38,732
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

997
00:55:38,815 --> 00:55:39,858
Here.

998
00:55:40,942 --> 00:55:42,277
[Isoo] Ham Sujeong?

999
00:55:43,570 --> 00:55:45,947
That name sounds familiar.

1000
00:55:46,031 --> 00:55:48,909
Ham Sujeong is...
[in English] "...Honey 7."

1001
00:55:49,868 --> 00:55:51,787
[in Korean] She's his only daughter,
born when he was 40.

1002
00:55:53,372 --> 00:55:54,373
[in English] Honey 7.

1003
00:55:54,456 --> 00:55:56,208
HONEY 7 HAM SUJEONG

1004
00:55:57,000 --> 00:55:58,210
[in Korean] We couldn't reach her.

1005
00:55:58,293 --> 00:56:01,088
Yes, she left for LA a week ago
and won't answer her phone.

1006
00:56:02,964 --> 00:56:05,425
His only daughter fell for a womanizer.

1007
00:56:05,509 --> 00:56:07,219
Of course he'd want to kill him.

1008
00:56:07,302 --> 00:56:10,305
Did he send his daughter to the US
and kill him while she was gone?

1009
00:56:13,975 --> 00:56:15,811
[taps table] I just got goosebumps.

1010
00:56:17,062 --> 00:56:20,023
His show was about Ham Sujeong.

1011
00:56:20,107 --> 00:56:23,527
There is someone I love.

1012
00:56:24,236 --> 00:56:25,737
She lived an unhappy life,

1013
00:56:25,821 --> 00:56:27,239
because her father

1014
00:56:28,657 --> 00:56:29,866
was a violent man.

1015
00:56:32,411 --> 00:56:35,080
[gasps] You're right. The violent father!

1016
00:56:35,163 --> 00:56:36,623
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1017
00:56:37,499 --> 00:56:39,876
He saw the performance three days prior

1018
00:56:40,460 --> 00:56:43,422
and planned to use
the casket in his murder?

1019
00:56:49,469 --> 00:56:52,681
He snuck backstage
and poured kerosene inside the casket.

1020
00:56:53,515 --> 00:56:54,683
Would that be possible?

1021
00:56:54,766 --> 00:56:56,351
I think it's possible.

1022
00:56:56,435 --> 00:56:59,980
But why didn't he just kill Park Jaeha
when he took him three days ago?

1023
00:57:00,564 --> 00:57:02,274
He was making a statement.

1024
00:57:03,066 --> 00:57:05,485
"Are you saying my daughter is
unhappy because of me?"

1025
00:57:06,361 --> 00:57:08,780
"Then I'll kill you for real on stage."

1026
00:57:08,864 --> 00:57:12,075
[♪ music swells, fades]

1027
00:57:12,159 --> 00:57:14,202
I can't get a location on Ham Seongwook.

1028
00:57:14,286 --> 00:57:15,829
And he won't answer his phone.

1029
00:57:15,912 --> 00:57:17,539
Did you find out his address?

1030
00:57:18,165 --> 00:57:19,166
Yes.

1031
00:57:19,249 --> 00:57:22,252
IDENTITY RECORD
HAM SEONGWOOK

1032
00:57:23,170 --> 00:57:24,755
Let's go and see what happens.

1033
00:57:25,422 --> 00:57:27,424
Detective Choi,
send Dr. Yoon the autopsy request.

1034
00:57:27,507 --> 00:57:28,592
Got it.

1035
00:57:28,675 --> 00:57:29,760
Jin Isoo, come with me.

1036
00:57:29,843 --> 00:57:32,179
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

1037
00:57:35,724 --> 00:57:38,852
[engine purrs, brakes squeal]

1038
00:57:41,188 --> 00:57:43,106
[♪ rock music sting plays, fades]

1039
00:57:50,363 --> 00:57:52,991
[doorbell chiming]

1040
00:57:55,869 --> 00:57:57,996
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

1041
00:57:58,079 --> 00:58:00,665
[doorbell chiming]

1042
00:58:00,749 --> 00:58:02,501
[Isoo] The lights are on.

1043
00:58:03,126 --> 00:58:04,753
[line connects, ringing]
STYLE
::cue()

1044
00:58:07,798 --> 00:58:09,049
[vehicle approaching]

1045
00:58:22,270 --> 00:58:23,271
[car door closes]

1046
00:58:25,023 --> 00:58:26,316
Can I help you?

1047
00:58:29,820 --> 00:58:30,862
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

1048
00:58:30,946 --> 00:58:32,531
It's him. The guy who kicked my seat.

1049
00:58:33,156 --> 00:58:35,075
-[exclaiming]
-Let go.

1050
00:58:36,451 --> 00:58:38,161
[exclaims in pain]

1051
00:58:39,913 --> 00:58:40,956
[groans]

1052
00:58:41,039 --> 00:58:42,123
What do you want?

1053
00:58:42,833 --> 00:58:44,417
We're with the police.

1054
00:58:45,085 --> 00:58:46,336
-Him, too?
-[scoffs]

1055
00:58:47,420 --> 00:58:48,421
Uh...

1056
00:58:49,047 --> 00:58:50,131
Yes, police.

1057
00:58:59,474 --> 00:59:00,809
No need to make a fuss. Go inside.

1058
00:59:01,518 --> 00:59:02,519
[henchman] Yes, sir.

1059
00:59:03,645 --> 00:59:05,564
-Get moving.
-Get back inside.

1060
00:59:11,069 --> 00:59:12,153
What's your name?

1061
00:59:16,449 --> 00:59:19,035
DIRECTOR BAEK CHULMIN

1062
00:59:19,119 --> 00:59:20,453
Mr. Baek Chulmin.

1063
00:59:21,580 --> 00:59:23,540
You were there
on the day Mr. Park Jaeha died.

1064
00:59:24,749 --> 00:59:25,917
It was a spectacular show.

1065
00:59:26,001 --> 00:59:27,252
He burned pretty well.

1066
00:59:27,335 --> 00:59:29,045
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1067
00:59:29,129 --> 00:59:30,463
Did you kill him?

1068
00:59:30,547 --> 00:59:31,590
[chuckles]

1069
00:59:31,673 --> 00:59:32,883
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1070
00:59:32,966 --> 00:59:34,467
You're barking up the wrong tree.

1071
00:59:35,260 --> 00:59:38,346
If I'd killed him,
you would never have found the body.

1072
00:59:38,722 --> 00:59:39,806
Hey...

1073
00:59:39,890 --> 00:59:40,974
He's lying.

1074
00:59:41,057 --> 00:59:42,684
His eyes shifted.

1075
00:59:42,767 --> 00:59:43,935
They're shifting.

1076
00:59:44,019 --> 00:59:45,312
[♪ music swells, stops]

1077
00:59:46,187 --> 00:59:47,230
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

1078
00:59:47,314 --> 00:59:49,608
Did you meet Mr. Park
three days before the incident?

1079
00:59:49,691 --> 00:59:52,277
-We had a chat.
-About what?

1080
00:59:52,360 --> 00:59:55,071
That bastard messed
with our boss's daughter.

1081
00:59:55,155 --> 00:59:58,033
So we just had a word with him.

1082
00:59:59,367 --> 01:00:02,871
Isn't it the Hammurabi way
to pay back in kind?

1083
01:00:03,288 --> 01:00:05,206
[scoffs] You've gone soft.

1084
01:00:06,207 --> 01:00:07,834
We need to meet Mr. Ham Seongwook.

1085
01:00:07,918 --> 01:00:09,544
-He's inside, right?
-The chairman

1086
01:00:10,545 --> 01:00:11,630
doesn't speak to cops.

1087
01:00:11,713 --> 01:00:12,756
[scoffs]

1088
01:00:12,839 --> 01:00:15,133
Everyone and their dog
is a chairman these days.

1089
01:00:15,216 --> 01:00:16,551
A chairman of what?

1090
01:00:16,635 --> 01:00:18,595
Of a makgeolli club? Huh?

1091
01:00:19,596 --> 01:00:20,722
What? Think I'm scared?

1092
01:00:20,805 --> 01:00:22,515
Let's end it here.

1093
01:00:22,599 --> 01:00:24,517
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

1094
01:00:25,310 --> 01:00:26,519
[sighs in exasperation]

1095
01:00:29,147 --> 01:00:32,317
Move your car,
and teach your kid how to behave.

1096
01:00:34,569 --> 01:00:36,780
-Kid? You're calling me a kid?
-[♪ music fades]

1097
01:00:36,863 --> 01:00:38,073
-[scoffs]
-[gate closes]

1098
01:00:38,657 --> 01:00:41,326
He's proud of being a thug, is that it?

1099
01:00:42,118 --> 01:00:44,037
Acting all tough. [clicks tongue]

1100
01:00:44,120 --> 01:00:46,456
I think we need to meet Ham Seongwook.

1101
01:00:47,165 --> 01:00:48,166
Call him in.

1102
01:00:48,249 --> 01:00:49,292
[sighs]

1103
01:00:49,376 --> 01:00:50,418
Like he'd come.

1104
01:00:51,795 --> 01:00:52,796
[Isoo groans]
STYLE
::cue()

1105
01:00:54,422 --> 01:00:56,967
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

1106
01:01:00,053 --> 01:01:02,597
FATHER AND DAUGHTER
HONEY 7 HAM SUJEONG, HAM SEONGWOOK

1107
01:01:04,933 --> 01:01:06,142
You're all working hard.

1108
01:01:06,977 --> 01:01:09,354
Here's the file on Ham Seongwook.

1109
01:01:09,437 --> 01:01:10,814
Go pay him a visit.

1110
01:01:10,897 --> 01:01:12,023
Okay, thank you.

1111
01:01:12,107 --> 01:01:14,025
-Thank you, sir!
-Thank you, sir!

1112
01:01:14,526 --> 01:01:15,694
[door opens]

1113
01:01:16,653 --> 01:01:17,737
[door closes]

1114
01:01:19,823 --> 01:01:23,493
Do we really have to go this far
just to meet a mob boss?

1115
01:01:24,369 --> 01:01:26,746
If he's refusing to cooperate,
he's hiding something.

1116
01:01:26,830 --> 01:01:27,831
We need to meet him fast.

1117
01:01:27,914 --> 01:01:30,083
MOVEMENT REPORT

1118
01:01:31,710 --> 01:01:35,672
HERITAGE SHOOTING CLUB
WEEKLY VISIT EVERY WEDNESDAY

1119
01:01:36,339 --> 01:01:37,549
Tomorrow's Wednesday.

1120
01:01:37,632 --> 01:01:39,259
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

1121
01:01:39,342 --> 01:01:40,552
I'll arrange a meeting.

1122
01:01:41,970 --> 01:01:43,346
Jin Isoo, what's going on?

1123
01:01:43,430 --> 01:01:45,265
Just sit back and relax for now.

1124
01:01:45,348 --> 01:01:46,433
I'll let you know.

1125
01:01:48,309 --> 01:01:49,728
What's with him?

1126
01:01:49,811 --> 01:01:52,814
He's thought of a way.
We just need to wait.

1127
01:01:56,985 --> 01:01:57,986
[♪ music fades]

1128
01:01:59,195 --> 01:02:00,280
DETECTIVE JIN ISOO

1129
01:02:00,363 --> 01:02:01,990
[cell phone vibrating]

1130
01:02:04,534 --> 01:02:05,744
[groans softly]

1131
01:02:08,121 --> 01:02:09,205
[grunts]

1132
01:02:09,289 --> 01:02:11,041
[cell phone continues vibrating]

1133
01:02:12,292 --> 01:02:13,293
[exhales softly]

1134
01:02:14,502 --> 01:02:15,795
Detective Jin.

1135
01:02:17,088 --> 01:02:18,381
[Isoo] Mr. Choi, are you busy?

1136
01:02:18,465 --> 01:02:19,758
No, I'm not.

1137
01:02:20,300 --> 01:02:21,509
What is it?

1138
01:02:21,593 --> 01:02:23,053
I have a favor to ask.

1139
01:02:24,179 --> 01:02:25,472
All right.

1140
01:02:26,306 --> 01:02:28,224
I'll get it taken care of right away.

1141
01:02:28,308 --> 01:02:30,602
Thank you. You're the best.

1142
01:02:31,853 --> 01:02:32,896
[chuckles softly]

1143
01:02:33,396 --> 01:02:34,397
Mr. Choi.

1144
01:02:35,023 --> 01:02:36,024
Yes?

1145
01:02:36,107 --> 01:02:38,026
Why do you sound so down?

1146
01:02:38,693 --> 01:02:40,904
I don't sound down at all.

1147
01:02:40,987 --> 01:02:42,655
You're not unwell, are you?

1148
01:02:42,739 --> 01:02:44,240
I'm fine.

1149
01:02:45,158 --> 01:02:46,409
Don't worry.

1150
01:02:47,535 --> 01:02:48,953
Okay, I'll leave that with you.

1151
01:02:49,662 --> 01:02:50,747
[sighs softly]

1152
01:02:52,415 --> 01:02:53,792
-[line disconnects]
-[sighs weekly]

1153
01:02:55,043 --> 01:02:57,045
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

1154
01:03:11,684 --> 01:03:14,395
HERITAGE SHOOTING CLUB

1155
01:03:36,417 --> 01:03:38,878
I'm sorry, but we are
unable to accommodate you today.

1156
01:03:39,712 --> 01:03:40,797
What do you mean?

1157
01:03:41,548 --> 01:03:42,924
He comes here every Wednesday.

1158
01:03:43,007 --> 01:03:44,300
I'm really sorry.

1159
01:03:44,843 --> 01:03:48,304
The truth is, the owner told us
not to let anyone in today.

1160
01:03:49,097 --> 01:03:51,808
The owner? You mean Mr. Park?

1161
01:03:52,684 --> 01:03:54,060
[club manager] Well,

1162
01:03:54,144 --> 01:03:56,771
the owner has changed as of today.
STYLE
::cue()

1163
01:03:56,855 --> 01:03:58,106
The guy's got no manners.

1164
01:03:58,898 --> 01:04:00,733
-Who is it?
-[Isoo] It's me.

1165
01:04:00,817 --> 01:04:02,610
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

1166
01:04:14,914 --> 01:04:16,291
[exhales smugly]

1167
01:04:16,666 --> 01:04:17,792
We finally get to meet.

1168
01:04:18,418 --> 01:04:19,878
Mr. Gangster, Ham Seongwook.

1169
01:04:22,881 --> 01:04:24,591
[♪ music swells]

1170
01:04:28,052 --> 01:04:29,387
[♪ music fades]

1171
01:04:31,389 --> 01:04:32,765
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

1172
01:04:40,023 --> 01:04:41,733
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1173
01:04:53,828 --> 01:04:55,121
[♪ music swells]

1174
01:04:59,667 --> 01:05:00,877
[gunshot]

1175
01:05:00,960 --> 01:05:02,420
[microphone feedback]

1176
01:05:02,503 --> 01:05:03,922
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1177
01:05:04,005 --> 01:05:05,215
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 7

1178
01:05:05,298 --> 01:05:06,591
A FACE-OFF WITH HAM SEONGWOOK!

1179
01:05:31,199 --> 01:05:34,619
Special Cast.
Son Woohyeon, Heo Sungtae, Jung Chaeyeon

1180
01:05:41,709 --> 01:05:43,836
-I won't ever see her again!
-Cut him.

1181
01:05:43,920 --> 01:05:45,129
[Sujeong] Dad.

1182
01:05:45,421 --> 01:05:46,422
Did you kill him?

1183
01:05:47,423 --> 01:05:49,008
Let's go back to the beginning.

1184
01:05:49,092 --> 01:05:50,301
[Kyungjin] I know who bought the kerosene.

1185
01:05:50,385 --> 01:05:51,427
[Hyera] That's Ms. Lee Jiyun.

1186
01:05:51,511 --> 01:05:53,721
[Junyoung] There was a kerosene heater
in the workshop.

1187
01:05:53,805 --> 01:05:55,932
[Hyera] He wanted to kill his brother
out of jealousy?

1188
01:05:56,015 --> 01:05:57,308
Were you in on it from the start?

1189
01:05:57,392 --> 01:05:59,519
-[Junyoung] Should start with this one.
-[Isoo, in English] Oh my god.

1190
01:06:00,103 --> 01:06:01,479
[in Korean] Pack up and leave quickly.

1191
01:06:01,562 --> 01:06:04,315
I can't return to the UK. [chuckles]

1192
01:06:04,399 --> 01:06:06,442
Two of Yu Seongwon's models disappeared.

1193
01:06:06,526 --> 01:06:08,861
-[bartender] Who is she?
-Someone obsessed with me.

1194
01:06:08,945 --> 01:06:11,698
I'm thinking of using her as a model.

1195
01:06:11,781 --> 01:06:13,574
[Isoo] You just need to use me.

1196
01:06:13,658 --> 01:06:15,743
-I'll do anything you need.
-[♪ music fades]

1197
01:06:18,162 --> 01:06:19,205
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1198
01:06:31,384 --> 01:06:32,510
Seven women?

1199
01:06:32,593 --> 01:06:34,512
[inhales sharply, exhales]

1200
01:06:34,595 --> 01:06:35,596
Yes.

1201
01:06:35,680 --> 01:06:36,931
[scoffs]

1202
01:06:37,015 --> 01:06:38,308
My Sujeong...

1203
01:06:39,017 --> 01:06:40,184
is... [in English] "Honey 7"?

1204
01:06:45,648 --> 01:06:46,983
[♪ music swells]

1205
01:06:50,236 --> 01:06:51,696
-[in Korean] Go bring that bastard in.
-[♪ music fades]

1206
01:06:51,779 --> 01:06:53,031
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

